  <p style="font-family: 'Times New Roman', Times, serif; font-size: 10pt; margin: 0pt; text-align: left">&#160;</p>
  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;text-indent:36pt;"><b>Interest Expense.</b> Total interest expense decreased $6.3 million, or 11.3%, for the year ended December 31, 2025, compared to the prior year, with decreases in deposit costs and borrowing costs of&#160;$5.4 million&#160;and&#160;$911,000, respectively. Deposit costs decreased primarily due to the lower average balance and rate paid on brokered CDs. The average cost of all interest-bearing deposit products decreased 30 basis points to 2.65% for the year ended December 31, 2025 from 2.95% for the year ended December 31, 2024. The average balances of money market, customer CD and savings accounts increased year-over-year, while lower cost&#160;transaction average account balances declined.&#160;Borrowing costs decreased 21 basis points, due to lower rates paid&#160;combined with a decrease of $6.4&#160;million in the average balance outstanding.</p>
  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;text-indent:36pt;">&#160;</p>
  <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;text-indent:36pt;">The following table details average balances, cost of funds and the change in interest expense for the periods shown:<b>&#160;</b></p>
