  <ix:nonNumeric contextRef="d_2025-01-01_2025-12-31" name="us-gaap:EarningsPerShareTextBlock" id="c3132875" escape="true">
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;"><b>Note <em style="font: inherit;">16</em>&#160;- Earnings per Common Share</b></p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;">The <em style="font: inherit;">two</em>-class method is used for&#160;computing basic and diluted earnings per share. Under the <em style="font: inherit;">two</em>-class method, EPS is determined for&#160;each class of common&#160;stock and participating security according to dividends declared and participating rights in undistributed earnings. The Company has issued restricted shares under share-based compensation plans which qualify as participating securities.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;">&#160;</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;">The following table presents a reconciliation of the components used to compute basic and diluted earnings per share for the periods shown.</p>
   <p style="font-family:'Times New Roman', Times, serif;font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;text-align:left;">&#160;</p>
